SUMMARY:Deadline: Co-GROWN: Biodesign Open Call 2026 (Bacterial Cellulose a
 nd Microbial Leather\, UK)
DESCRIPTION:Co-GROWN is a biodesign competition run by the Tom Ellis synthe
 tic biology lab at Imperial College London\, Northumbria University's Livi
 ng Construction group and KY Labs\, centred on bacterial cellulose and bio
 logically integrated colour systems\, specifically self-dyed microbial lea
 ther grown by microbial co-cultures that produce material and colour simul
 taneously. Entrants respond with commercially relevant design proposals us
 ing a curated bacterial cellulose material library. WHAT YOU GET: the winn
 er receives up to GBP 10\,000 towards prototype development with the synth
 etic-biology and living-construction research groups\, plus access to spec
 ialist labs and biofabrication facilities\, mentorship\, and publication\,
  exhibition and showcase opportunities\; finalists join the network with e
 xhibition\, publication\, mentoring and research or internship collaborati
 on prospects. ELIGIBILITY: emerging designers\, architects\, artists and m
 akers\, material researchers and students\, individuals or teams\, interna
 tionally. DEADLINE: 26 October 2026 per the site's key dates (the site's d
 ate block contains typos\, so double-check on the page before applying).\n
 \nOrganisation: Imperial College London (Tom Ellis Lab)\, Northumbria Univ
 ersity (Living Construction group) and KY Labs\nLocation: International op
 en call\; prototype development at Northumbria University facilities\, UK.
 \nAward: Winner receives up to GBP 10\,000 towards prototype development\,
  plus access to specialist labs and biofabrication facilities\, mentorship
  from leading biodesign researchers\, and publication\, exhibition and sho
 wcase opportunities. Finalists get exhibition\, publication and mentoring.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Development through to the winner announce
 ment in May 2027\; judging January 2027.\n\nMore: https://co-grown.design/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
